  const overview=()=>`<main class="page-content overview-page"><section class="hero-row live-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="live-pip"></span> FIELD ATLAS&nbsp; / &nbsp;THANE, MAHARASHTRA</div><h1>Thane,<br><em>under the sun.</em></h1><p class="hero-intro">An animated city study, coloured by live weather. Orbit the model or switch to satellite imagery to explore the places behind the pattern.</p></div><div class="hero-aside"><span class="hero-aside-label">ON THE MAP</span><b>3D city study<br>Live weather</b><span data-updated>Connecting to Thane…</span></div></section><section class="live-metrics" aria-label="Current weather in Thane"><div class="weather-deck-note">THANE / NOW</div><article><span>Air temperature</span><strong data-live-temp>—°</strong><small>Thane · 2 m above ground</small></article><article><span>Feels like</span><strong data-live-apparent>—°</strong><small>Model-derived apparent temperature</small></article><article><span>Humidity</span><strong data-live-humidity>—%</strong><small>Current weather model</small></article><article><span>Wind</span><strong data-live-wind>—</strong><small>10 m · km/h</small></article></section><section class="forecast-panel" aria-labelledby="forecastTitle"><div class="forecast-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">NEXT 24 HOURS / MAJIWADA MODEL GRID</span><h2 id="forecastTitle">Plan around the heat.</h2></div><span data-forecast-summary>Forecast loading…</span></div><div class="forecast-chart" data-forecast-chart><div class="forecast-empty">The next 24 hours will appear when the weather feed connects.</div></div><div class="forecast-times" data-forecast-times></div><div class="forecast-foot">Open-Meteo forecast · regional model estimate, not a street-level measurement</div></section><section class="overview-grid"><div class="map-panel panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">SATELLITE VIEW / THANE</span><h2>Heat, seen at city scale.</h2></div><span class="map-tag">Imagery · Esri</span></div><div class="map-toolbar" role="group" aria-label="City view"><button class="map-layer is-active" data-map-layer="city3d">3D city</button><button class="map-layer" data-map-layer="imagery">Satellite</button><button class="map-layer" data-map-layer="weather">Readings</button></div><div class="map-wrap satellite-map-wrap city-view-stage" id="cityView" data-layer="city3d"><div id="city3dScene" class="is-active" aria-label="Animated 3D city model of Thane with live weather heat fields"><div class="city3d-loading"><span></span><b>Building a city view</b></div><div class="city3d-meta"><span>THANE / 3D STUDY</span><span>Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom</span></div></div><div class="map-wrap satellite-map-view" id="satelliteMap" data-layer="heat" role="application" aria-label="Interactive satellite map of Thane with weather-derived heat contours"><div class="map-loading"><span class="map-loading-orbit"></span><b>Opening satellite view</b><small>Esri imagery · Thane, Maharashtra</small></div></div><div class="map-legend satellite-legend"><span>Cooler</span><i></i><span>Warmer</span></div><div class="map-note" data-map-source>Thane city study · weather-tinted</div></div><div class="map-caption"><span data-map-caption>3D city study, not surveyed building geometry. Heat tint follows regional weather-model values.</span><a href="evidence.html">Sources & method <b>↗</b></a></div></div><aside class="area-panel panel live-points-panel"><div class="area-panel-top"><span class="eyebrow">WEATHER POINTS</span><span class="area-rank" data-point-count>0 / 07</span></div><div class="area-name-wrap"><h2>Across Thane</h2><span class="area-zone">Tap a place to zoom into its heat field</span></div><div class="hotspot-tools"><button class="text-button" data-sort-hotspots aria-pressed="false">Rank hottest first ↕</button><button class="text-button" data-export-weather>Export CSV ↓</button></div><div class="heat-alert"><label><input type="checkbox" data-alert-toggle> <span>Alert me above</span></label><strong><span data-alert-value>36</span>° feels like</strong><input type="range" min="30" max="45" value="36" step="1" data-alert-threshold aria-label="Feels-like alert threshold in Celsius"><small data-alert-status>Local alert · this device only</small></div><div class="favorite-tools"><button class="text-button" data-save-favorite>☆ Save selected place</button><select data-favorite-select aria-label="Saved favorite places"><option value="">Saved places…</option></select></div><div class="heat-alert-message" data-alert-message hidden role="status"></div><div class="weather-point-list">${[['thane-west','Thane West'],['majiwada','Majiwada'],['naupada','Naupada'],['wagle-estate','Wagle Estate'],['kalwa','Kalwa'],['kasarvadavali','Kasarvadavali'],['ghodbunder','Ghodbunder Road']].map(([id,name])=>`<button class="weather-point" data-weather-focus="${id}"><span class="weather-point-dot"></span><b>${name}</b><strong data-weather-temp="${id}">—°</strong><small data-weather-feels="${id}">loading</small></button>`).join('')}</div><p class="weather-source-note">Open-Meteo model values at these coordinates. The model grid is regional; it does not resolve street-level temperature.</p><button class="button button-primary" data-map-refresh>Refresh live readings <span>↻</span></button><small class="panel-footnote" data-live-timestamp>Awaiting first update…</small></aside></section><section class="bottom-grid"><article class="section-card"><div class="section-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">A CLOSER LOOK</span><h2>Shade changes the walk.</h2></div><a href="cooling-studio.html" class="arrow-link">BUILD A SCENARIO ↗</a></div><div class="lever-list"><div><span class="lever-icon icon-tree">✳</span><div><b>Grow continuous shade</b><small>Connect tree canopy along walking routes.</small></div><span class="lever-count">01</span></div><div><span class="lever-icon icon-roof">◩</span><div><b>Reflect more rooftop heat</b><small>Test cool-roof coverage as an area scenario.</small></div><span class="lever-count">02</span></div><div><span class="lever-icon icon-center">⌂</span><div><b>Map potential cool spaces</b><small>Candidate locations need on-ground verification.</small></div><span class="lever-count">03</span></div></div></article><article class="quote-card"><span class="eyebrow">A NOTE FROM THE ATLAS</span><p>“Shade changes the walk.<br><em>Small shifts add up.</em>”</p><span>THANE FIELD ATLAS · WEATHER UPDATED THROUGHOUT THE DAY</span></article></section></main>`;
  const neighborhoodPage=()=>`<main class="page-content"><section class="subpage-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="live-pip"></span> ${pageTitle} / THANE SAMPLE AREAS</div><h1>The city, <em>area by area.</em></h1><p>Browse the sample areas and compare the assumptions behind each one. These are not surveyed boundaries or measured heat readings.</p></div><a class="button button-secondary" href="evidence.html">Read the method <span>↗</span></a></section><section class="explorer-grid"><div class="map-panel panel explorer-map"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">SAMPLE AREA VIEW</span><h2>Select a sample area.</h2></div><span class="map-tag">DEMO / NOT TO SCALE</span></div><div class="map-wrap" data-layer="exposure">${mapSvg()}<div class="map-note">SYNTHETIC PROXIES / NO OFFICIAL BOUNDARIES</div></div></div><aside class="explorer-detail panel"><span class="eyebrow">AREA DETAIL / <span data-detail-code>01</span></span><h2 data-area-name>Majiwada</h2><span class="area-zone" data-area-zone>Growth corridor</span><div class="detail-score"><strong data-area-index>73</strong><span>relative exposure index<br><small>illustrative / 0–100</small></span></div><p data-area-note>A high-build scenario area for testing shade and roof options.</p><div class="area-bars"><div><span>Green-cover proxy</span><b data-green>25%</b><i><em data-green-bar style="width:25%"></em></i></div><div><span>Built-up proxy</span><b data-built>84%</b><i><em data-built-bar style="width:84%"></em></i></div><div><span>Shade proxy</span><b data-shade>31%</b><i><em data-shade-bar style="width:31%"></em></i></div></div><button class="button button-primary" data-plan-area>Use in Cooling Studio <span>↗</span></button></aside></section><section class="area-directory panel"><div class="directory-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">AREA DIRECTORY</span><h2>Compare the sample set.</h2></div><label class="search-field"><span>⌕</span><input id="areaSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search area name" aria-label="Search areas"></label></div><div class="area-table-head"><span>AREA / SAMPLE LABEL</span><span>ZONE TYPE</span><span>EXPOSURE PROXY</span><span>GREEN PROXY</span><span></span></div><div id="areaRows" class="area-rows">${areas.map((a,i)=>`<button class="area-row ${a.id==='majiwada'?'selected':''}" data-area-select="${a.id}"><span><i class="zone-dot ${a.accent}"></i><b>${a.name}</b></span><span>${a.zone}</span><span><b>${a.index}</b><i class="mini-bar"><em style="width:${a.index}%"></em></i></span><span>${a.green}%</span><span class="row-arrow">↗</span></button>`).join('')}</div><p class="table-footnote">All proxy figures shown here are synthetic UI demo values. No neighborhood ranking should be used for decisions.</p></section></main>`;
  const studioPage=()=>`<main class="page-content"><section class="subpage-hero studio-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="live-pip"></span> COOLING STUDIO / SCENARIO BUILDER</div><h1>Make room<br><em>for shade.</em></h1><p>Try a cooling plan for one of Thane’s sample areas. Adjust the interventions and see how the illustrative index responds.</p></div><div class="scenario-badge"><span>SCENARIO</span><b>LOCAL<br>ONLY</b><i>NO API KEY</i></div></section><section class="studio-layout"><div class="studio-controls panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / SET THE SCENE</span><h2>Choose your levers.</h2></div><button class="text-button" data-reset>Reset ↺</button></div><label class="select-label">SAMPLE AREA<select id="studioArea">${areas.map(a=>`<option value="${a.id}" ${a.id==='majiwada'?'selected':''}>${a.name} · sample area</option>`).join('')}</select></label><div class="intervention-list"><label class="intervention-row"><input type="checkbox" data-intervention="trees" checked><span class="intervention-glyph tree-glyph">✳</span><span><b>Street shade + tree canopy</b><small>Grow shade along selected routes</small></span><span class="toggle-ui"></span></label><label class="intervention-row"><input type="checkbox" data-intervention="roofs" checked><span class="intervention-glyph roof-glyph">◩</span><span><b>Reflective roof coverage</b><small>Test cool-roof treatment across blocks</small></span><span class="toggle-ui"></span></label><label class="intervention-row"><input type="checkbox" data-intervention="cooling" checked><span class="intervention-glyph center-glyph">⌂</span><span><b>Potential cool spaces</b><small>Add candidate centers for verification</small></span><span class="toggle-ui"></span></label><label class="intervention-row"><input type="checkbox" data-intervention="routes"><span class="intervention-glyph route-glyph">↗</span><span><b>Shaded walking links</b><small>Connect key destinations with shade</small></span><span class="toggle-ui"></span></label></div><label class="range-row"><span><b>Scenario budget</b><strong><output id="budgetValue">42</output> units</strong></span><input type="range" id="budgetRange" min="10" max="100" value="42"><small>Relative planning units only; not rupees or a cost estimate.</small></label><div class="scenario-name-field"><label for="scenarioName">Save this scenario as</label><input id="scenarioName" maxlength="36" value="Shade-first mix" placeholder="e.g. Shade-first mix"></div><div class="studio-actions"><button class="button button-primary" data-save-scenario>Save scenario <span>＋</span></button><button class="button button-secondary" data-export>Export JSON ↓</button></div><div id="studioToast" class="inline-toast" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div></div><div class="studio-results"><article class="scenario-map panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">PLAN / SAMPLE VIEW</span><h2 data-studio-area>Majiwada</h2></div><span class="map-tag">SIMULATED</span></div><div class="map-wrap scenario-map-wrap" data-layer="exposure">${mapSvg()}<div class="map-note">COOLING LEVERS / HYPOTHETICAL OVERLAY</div></div></article><article class="result-panel panel"><div class="result-title"><span class="eyebrow">SCENARIO / RELATIVE INDEX</span><span class="scenario-live"><i></i> UPDATING</span></div><div class="result-main"><span>Relative exposure proxy</span><strong data-result-index>58</strong><small data-result-delta>−15 pts from sample baseline</small></div><div class="result-bars"><div><span>Shade continuity</span><b data-result-shade>56%</b><i><em data-result-shade-bar style="width:56%"></em></i></div><div><span>Option coverage index</span><b data-result-coverage>47%</b><i><em data-result-coverage-bar style="width:47%"></em></i></div></div><div class="result-disclaimer">Toy scenario formula · relative index points only · not °C, population counts, engineering advice, or measured impact.</div></article></div></section><section class="saved-section"><div class="section-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">SAVED HERE</span><h2>Saved plans.</h2></div><span class="local-badge">SAVED ON THIS DEVICE</span></div><div id="savedScenarios" class="saved-grid"></div><div class="compare-panel panel" id="comparePanel" hidden></div><p class="table-footnote">Saved scenarios stay in this browser. They are not sent to a server.</p></section></main>`;
  const evidencePage=()=>`<main class="page-content"><section class="subpage-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="live-pip"></span> EVIDENCE / METHOD / LIMITS</div><h1>Every layer<br><em>has a source.</em></h1><p>A plain-language record of the data behind the atlas, what each source can tell us, and where the gaps remain.</p></div><span class="evidence-stamp">OPEN<br>METHOD</span></section><section class="evidence-status panel"><div class="status-copy"><span class="eyebrow">DATA, AS IT STANDS</span><h2>Live weather context plus illustrative scenarios.</h2><p>The city view now uses live Open-Meteo weather-model readings and Esri satellite imagery. Weather grid values are broad-scale ambient conditions, not measured neighborhood surface temperatures. Other area shapes and cooling scenarios remain illustrative until validated local datasets are connected.</p></div><div class="status-count"><strong>01</strong><span>live weather source<br>connected · 07 points</span></div></section><section class="source-section"><div class="section-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / CONNECTED + CANDIDATE DATA REGISTER</span><h2>Free sources, with context.</h2></div><span class="source-count">${sourceItems.length} DATA SOURCES</span></div><div class="source-list">${sourceItems.map((s,i)=>`<article class="source-card panel"><span class="source-number">0${i+1}</span><div class="source-info"><span class="source-kind">${s.kind}</span><h3>${s.name}</h3><small>${s.owner}</small></div><div class="source-limit"><b>${s.status}</b><p>${s.limit}</p></div><a href="${s.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="source-link" aria-label="Open ${s.name} source">↗</a></article>`).join('')}</div></section><section class="method-grid"><article class="method-card"><span>02 / CALCULATION</span><h3>Start with a baseline.</h3><p>Use a transparent vegetation/built-up proxy first. Compare its rankings to available observations before adding more complex models.</p></article><article class="method-card"><span>03 / SCENARIO MODEL</span><h3>State every assumption.</h3><p>Cooling levers modify a relative demo index through an intentionally simple formula. Outputs are not temperatures, people served, or a costed plan.</p></article><article class="method-card"><span>04 / EVALUATION</span><h3>Try to break the result.</h3><p>Hold out dates or locations where observations exist. Test whether intervention rankings change when weights, missing data, and assumptions change.</p></article></section><section class="limits-band"><span class="limits-icon">!</span><div><b>Not an emergency alert or medical guidance.</b><p>Use IMD and local authorities for current warnings. HeatShield’s future maps require review and field validation before supporting real-world decisions.</p></div><a href="https://mausam.imd.gov.in/responsive/heatwave_guidance.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IMD guidance ↗</a></section></main>`;
